---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../../lib/site";
import { localizePath , pick } from "../../i18n/utils";

const lang = (Astro.currentLocale ?? "en") as "en" | "zh";

const slug = "workspaces-and-tabs";

const C = pick({
  en: {
    heading: "Workspaces, environments, and tabs",
    intro:
      "Workspaces and environments keep your servers organized, while connection tabs let you run more than one session at once. Here is how the pieces fit together.",
    meta: "Documentation",
    title: "Workspaces, environments, and tabs — VVTerm",
    description:
      "Organize servers with workspaces and environments in VVTerm, run multiple sessions with connection tabs, and understand the free and Pro tier limits.",
    schemaDescription:
      "How VVTerm organizes servers with workspaces and environments, how connection tabs let you run multiple sessions, and the free and Pro limits that apply.",
    bodyHtml: `
  <p>
    As you add more machines, VVTerm gives you two ways to keep them organized — workspaces and
    environments — and connection tabs so you can work in several sessions at once. They sync across
    your devices through iCloud, so your organization is the same everywhere.
  </p>

  <h2>Workspaces</h2>
  <p>
    A <strong>workspace</strong> is the top-level group your servers belong to. Use one per client, per
    project, or per team to keep unrelated machines apart. Every server lives inside exactly one
    workspace, and switching workspaces changes which servers you see. Workspaces sync through iCloud
    along with the servers they contain.
  </p>

  <h2>Environments</h2>
  <p>
    Within a workspace, an <strong>environment</strong> sorts servers further — for example Production,
    Staging, or Development. Environments let you filter a busy list down to the machines you care
    about right now, and they keep production hosts visually distinct from the ones you can experiment
    on. You set a server's environment when <a href="/docs/adding-a-server">adding or editing it</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Connection tabs</h2>
  <p>
    A <strong>connection tab</strong> is a single live session with a server. Opening a server starts a
    tab; opening another server, or the same server again, starts a second tab. Each tab is independent,
    so you can run a long task in one while you work in another.
  </p>
  <p>
    Switch between tabs to move from one session to the next without disconnecting. On Mac, tabs live in
    the unified toolbar; on iPhone and iPad you move between your open connections from the session view.
  </p>

  <h2>Free and Pro limits</h2>
  <p>VVTerm's tiers control how much you can organize and how many sessions you can run at once:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Free</strong> — one workspace, one server, and one connection tab.</li>
    <li><strong>Pro</strong> — unlimited workspaces, servers, and connection tabs.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    With Pro you can keep several connections open at the same time — for example a production shell, a
    staging shell, and an SFTP session — and group them across as many workspaces and environments as
    you need. Pro is <strong>$6.49 per month</strong> or <strong>$24.99 per year</strong>, with a
    one-time <strong>lifetime</strong> purchase at <strong>$49.99</strong>; billing and refunds are
    handled by Apple.
  </p>

  <h2>Next steps</h2>
  <p>
    Start by <a href="/docs/adding-a-server">adding a server</a> and placing it in a workspace, then
    learn how your organization travels between devices in <a href="/docs/icloud-sync">iCloud sync and Keychain</a>.
  </p>
`,
  },
  zh: {
    heading: "工作区、环境与标签页",
    intro:
      "工作区和环境让你的服务器井然有序，而连接标签页让你同时运行不止一个会话。这里说明这些组成部分如何配合。",
    meta: "文档",
    title: "工作区、环境与标签页 — VVTerm",
    description:
      "在 VVTerm 中用工作区和环境整理服务器，用连接标签页运行多个会话，并了解免费版和 Pro 版的限制。",
    schemaDescription:
      "VVTerm 如何用工作区和环境整理服务器、连接标签页如何让你运行多个会话，以及适用的免费版和 Pro 版限制。",
    bodyHtml: `
  <p>
    随着你添加更多机器，VVTerm 给了你两种保持它们井然有序的方式 —— 工作区和环境 —— 以及连接标签页，让你能同时在多个会话中工作。它们通过 iCloud 在你的设备间同步，因此你的组织方式在任何地方都一样。
  </p>

  <h2>工作区</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>工作区</strong>是你的服务器所归属的顶层分组。为每个客户、每个项目或每个团队使用一个工作区，把不相关的机器分开。每台服务器都恰好位于一个工作区内，切换工作区会改变你看到的服务器。工作区会连同它们包含的服务器一起通过 iCloud 同步。
  </p>

  <h2>环境</h2>
  <p>
    在工作区内，<strong>环境</strong>进一步对服务器排序 —— 例如 Production、Staging 或 Development。环境让你把繁忙的列表筛选到你此刻关心的机器，并让生产主机在视觉上与你可以实验的机器区分开。你在<a href="/zh/docs/adding-a-server">添加或编辑服务器</a>时设置它的环境。
  </p>

  <h2>连接标签页</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>连接标签页</strong>是与某台服务器的单个实时会话。打开一台服务器会启动一个标签页；打开另一台服务器、或再次打开同一台服务器，会启动第二个标签页。每个标签页都是独立的，因此你可以在一个里运行长时间任务，同时在另一个里工作。
  </p>
  <p>
    在标签页之间切换可以在不断开连接的情况下从一个会话移到下一个。在 Mac 上，标签页位于统一工具栏中；在 iPhone 和 iPad 上，你从会话视图在打开的连接之间移动。
  </p>

  <h2>免费版与 Pro 限制</h2>
  <p>VVTerm 的分级控制你能整理多少内容、能同时运行多少会话：</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>免费版</strong> —— 一个工作区、一台服务器、一个连接标签页。</li>
    <li><strong>Pro</strong> —— 无限工作区、服务器和连接标签页。</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    使用 Pro，你可以同时打开多个连接 —— 例如一个生产 shell、一个预发 shell 和一个 SFTP 会话 —— 并把它们分组到任意多的工作区和环境中。Pro 为<strong>每月 $6.49</strong> 或<strong>每年 $24.99</strong>，另有一次性<strong>终身</strong>买断 <strong>$49.99</strong>；计费和退款由 Apple 处理。
  </p>

  <h2>后续步骤</h2>
  <p>
    先从<a href="/zh/docs/adding-a-server">添加服务器</a>并把它放入工作区开始，然后在<a href="/zh/docs/icloud-sync">iCloud 同步与 Keychain</a>中了解你的组织方式如何在设备间流转。
  </p>
`,
  },
}, lang);

const articleSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "TechArticle",
  name: C.heading,
  description: C.schemaDescription,
  url: `${SITE.siteUrl}${localizePath(`/docs/${slug}`, lang)}`,
};
---

<DocsLayout
  kind="docs"
  activeSlug={slug}
  heading={C.heading}
  intro={C.intro}
  meta={C.meta}
  title={C.title}
  description={C.description}
  canonicalPath={`/docs/${slug}`}
  structuredData={[articleSchema]}
>
  <Fragment set:html={C.bodyHtml} />
</DocsLayout>
